From cf3642cef081a35ac30c44d736fe1a9995ef0115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:21:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09309/11362] Widen the gate-blindness record: 7 of 13 games,
 not 4 of 7

An initial sweep over the 7 cached windows on disk put the blast radius at 4 of 7.
window_meta.json covers 13 games and gives 7 blind: sb26 at 9 transitions and six games
at 12, against six games at 3 to 5 that the gate can see. The threshold is exact -- the
win frame sits at grid index 2n-1 against a 12-grid probe cap, so the gate sees it only
for n <= 6.

The blind set is the long-window games, which are the ones where induction is hardest
and a working goal predicate is worth the most.

Recorded but not verified: six of the seven blind games sit at exactly 12 transitions,
which looks like a builder cap rather than a coincidence. If so, every capped window is
exactly twice the probe's reach -- 12 transitions is 24 grids, the probe covers 12. No
such constant was found by grep, and sb26 at 9 shows not every long window hits it.

This half of the finding is arithmetic over window length, so unlike the effect size it
is not scoped to the generator.

